Here's the full combined rundown — organized so you can work through it as an actual task list. I've grouped by severity, and added a cross-cutting section at the end for issues that only show up when you look at frontend + backend together.

🔴 BACKEND — Critical
 Soft-delete vs unique index conflict — email, sku, referenceNo, and unique name fields (Category/Unit/Role/Permission) will throw E11000 when a user tries to recreate something that was soft-deleted. Fix: partial unique indexes ({ deletedAt: null } filter) or suffix-on-delete.
 No transactions on receivePurchaseOrder / adjustStock — parallel Promise.all with partial failure leaves stock/movement ledger inconsistent, and retries double-apply. Wrap in mongoose.startSession().withTransaction(). Requires replica-set MongoDB (Atlas has this by default; local dev needs single-node replica set).
 confirmTokenExpires typed as String — verify the expiry comparison is actually parsing to Date, not doing a string compare that happens to work by luck with ISO format.
🟠 BACKEND — High Priority
 Purchase cancel doesn't reverse stock — either implement reversal for received→cancelled transitions, or remove the vestigial purchase_cancel StockMovement type/docs so it stops implying behavior that doesn't exist.
 ?search= 500s on non-Product resources — make APIFeatures.filter() silently drop search when the model has no text index, instead of letting Mongo throw a raw 500.
 my-* endpoints have no pagination — myPurchases/myAdjustments/myMovements/myAudits will eventually choke on power users with thousands of records. Route them through the same APIFeatures pipeline as getAll*.
 generatePurchaseRef count-based race — replace count-then-insert with an atomic findOneAndUpdate on a Counter collection to remove the collision entirely instead of retrying around it.
 Wire up getInventoryDashboard — it already exists and is correct except for one bug (see below); mounting it as a real endpoint removes the frontend's client-side approximation entirely (see cross-cutting section).
🟡 BACKEND — Medium
 getInventoryDashboard doesn't filter soft-deleted products — fix before wiring it up (see above).
 Cache invalidation is manual per-handler — easy to forget on new write paths. Consider inferring the resource from req.baseUrl in a wrapper so it can't be missed.
 Retroactive costPrice overwrite on purchase receive — silently rewrites historical stockValue. Store unitCostAtReceipt per movement if you ever want accurate margin history.
 No idempotency key on POST /purchases/make — double-click or client retry-on-timeout creates duplicate POs. Pairs naturally with the transaction work above.
 Mount Swagger — app.use('/api-docs', swaggerUi.serve, swaggerUi.setup(swaggerSpec)). 5-minute fix, high payoff for frontend/API consumers.
 Compound indexes — Product likely needs {category, status} or {status, currentStock} compound indexes matching real dashboard/filter query patterns, not just single-field indexes.
🟢 BACKEND — Low / Cleanup
 Delete/prune dead code: restrictTo, isLoggedIn, unused createUser, unused getInventoryDashboard (once wired up, no longer dead).
 Standardize response shapes: deleteProduct (204 no body) vs deleteRole/deleteSupplier (204 + ignored JSON body); getAllRoles top-level length vs nested elsewhere.
